EasyFly modifications (2026-10-19): distinct class/library; reject a missing ROS
node; disconnect update callback before teardown; publish a single ImuMessage
snapshot including its measurement stamp instead of scheduler LastUpdateTime and
separate getters. Skip uninitialized/byte-identical snapshots, never retimestamp,
interpolate, fill a source gap, or suppress a backwards/conflicting measurement.
Reliable publisher history is bounded at 1000 by default (upstream: 5), matching
the guard reader so transient shared-image transport pressure need not exhaust
the writer history. Sensor physics, configured rate, frame, noise and covariance
are unchanged.
Optional bounded producer timing records CLOCK_MONOTONIC callback/snapshot/publish
boundaries in memory and writes CSV at teardown; disabled by default. It does not
alter the ROS message or measurement timestamp.
